In my experience it's not that R is the problem, but that you can't
expect the usual algorithms to nicely deal with enormous data sets.  If
you do the 2-d binning yourself, ggplot offers some nice ways to plot a
heat map to summarize that, but it won't succeed in doing the binning
for you.

For strategies, have you tried doing the summary with one of the 2-d
density/binning functions?  A 17 million point scatterplot won't carry
any more information for a person looking at it than a heatmap of the
density approximation.  Even then you will probably have to look at
different packages that implement binning to find one that works on your
scale, and fiddle with the parameters.

Krzysztof

